    {
      "id": "claim_e00276062598484e92094b7fec713a84",
      "statement": "The repository has no root requirements.txt; a previously checked-in frozen pip-freeze file by that name was deleted because its pins were mutually unsatisfiable and it was the source of 136 of 142 open Dependabot alerts against code that no build or deploy path ever consumed. pyproject.toml + uv.lock remain the sole application dependency source, and contributors must not restore or use a root requirements.txt; the unrelated tests/server/oracle/requirements.txt, which pins an isolated oracle test environment, is preserved and is not a substitute.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/decisions/dependabot-requirements-txt.md",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:f0631b2e7733bba312080af2b480b04c9a045949652ddb77cc061adb264a83d3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b4b212b81565428388821f8fa7749bf0",
      "statement": "`make test` runs offline pytest (evaluator calibration, privacy/routing/graph suites under tests/graph/, safety gate, and parity gate) with no network access by default (pytest addopts excludes the `judge` marker); `make test-judges` runs the LLM-judge calibration tests (`-m judge`), which call OpenAI and need OPENAI_API_KEY.",
      "evidence": [
