    {
      "id": "claim_7b68a44f57ba41beae5729d8eb397244",
      "statement": "There is no `make lint` or `make type-check` target; static analysis is run ad hoc via `uv run ruff check <paths>` and `uv run basedpyright <paths>`. The scripted quality gate (scripts/verify/f2_quality.sh) deliberately scopes ruff and basedpyright to healthcare_rag/agent plus a short, explicit list of evals/, tests/agent, and scripts/ files rather than the whole repository, because the rest of the codebase predates ruff/basedpyright adoption and is not retroactively linted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/verify/AGENTS.md#L18-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:039bb10d1dd1544b20b7880d6b4f5bc15b76663602b6809609af7dc35094f505:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/verify/f2_quality.sh#L1-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f68d6803291fae11c58905b81f4d3cf82f222bf83e1baea9cf4e150d1da4a261:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f88f07dc01874a16b0fb0cb7bc751a2b",
      "statement": "The Makefile exposes a graduated set of eval commands: `make eval-smoke` (3-example fast smoke), `make eval PREFIX=name` (full golden-set eval with LLM judges), `make eval-nojudge PREFIX=name` (full deterministic-only, cheapest), `make eval-holdout` (hold-out split), `make eval-ablations` (stage ablations: no-validate/no-evaluate/no-decompose via HC_RAG_DISABLE_STAGES), `make eval-multiturn`/`make eval-multiturn-smoke` (multi-turn conversation eval), and `make compare EXPS=\"a b c\"` (side-by-side experiment comparison); full judge evals are recommended only after corpus/model/prompt safety changes, with eval-smoke or a filtered deterministic run used for ordinary code changes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Makefile#L78-L96",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:58e4fd67e0073bd3c54cef295829724b5b55211eccdc29943287ba3fa7a1e361:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9255791248db4eadbaecb5485a46e96e",
      "statement": "This runbook's Make-target and CLI behaviors are compiled from static inspection of the Makefile, docker-compose.yml, pyproject.toml, and CLI/storage source rather than from a live execution of `make venv`/`make weaviate`/`make ingest`/`make run`/`make test`/eval commands in the authoring session; the closest available empirical corroboration is docs/decisions/dependabot-requirements-txt.md recording that the full offline test suite was actually run against the current dependency graph, and scripts/verify/f2_quality.sh, which is itself an executable pass/fail gate (make test, scoped ruff, scoped basedpyright, frontend build/test) rather than descriptive documentation.",
